I audited the uploaded source as a **pre-production release candidate** and also checked the current 2026 Google, ASIC and OAIC guidance relevant to your goals.

My overall assessment: **the architecture is much closer to production-ready than it was earlier, but I would not call this a green production release yet.** The biggest remaining work is not another redesign. It is release verification, content depth/authority, compliance review, privacy accuracy, mobile QA, and proving the live deployment behaves exactly as the source intends.

One important expectation to set: no legitimate SEO work can guarantee “1000% retention” or a top Google position. Google explicitly emphasizes helpful, reliable, people-first, original content rather than content primarily made to manipulate rankings. Its 2026 guidance for AI-powered Search likewise stresses valuable, unique, non-commodity content. ([Google Developers][1])

