# 9. Privacy page needs more precision

Your Privacy Policy is substantially better than many early-stage sites.

It discloses:

* account data;
* session data;
* affiliate-click data;
* GA;
* cookies;
* embedded videos;
* approximate location/device/browser information;
* service providers;
* security;
* access/correction;
* OAIC escalation.

OAIC itself publicly discloses Google Analytics collection including pages visited, timestamps, device/browser information and approximate geographic data. ([OAIC][5])

But your section:

> “Sharing and overseas disclosure”

only says data may be processed by hosting/database providers and Google.

I'd review whether it should identify **likely overseas processing locations/providers** more precisely based on your actual deployment architecture.

Also document:

* Vercel;
* Supabase/Postgres hosting region;
* Google Analytics;
* authentication infrastructure;
* embedded YouTube/Vimeo behavior;
* email provider;
* logs;
* retention periods;
* deletion/account closure behavior.

OAIC's updated APP guidance also emphasizes data minimisation—collecting only what is reasonably necessary. ([OAIC][6])

Your analytics design is already relatively conservative because you're intentionally not sending names/email/financial form values to GA.

Keep it that way.

