# 10. Don't call content “human-built” just because AI wasn't visible

Your last requirement is important:

> all contents should be human building not AI way

I'd define this operationally rather than stylistically.

Google's guidance is about **value and purpose**, not merely whether AI touched the drafting process. It emphasizes original information, reporting, research and analysis. ([Google Developers][1])

Your publishing workflow should therefore require:

```text
Topic selected because users need it
            ↓
Primary-source research
            ↓
Human outline
            ↓
Draft
            ↓
Facts linked to sources
            ↓
Worked examples / diagrams / tools
            ↓
Australian context
            ↓
Human editorial review
            ↓
Compliance-language review
            ↓
SEO review
            ↓
Publish
            ↓
Scheduled factual re-verification
```

AI can assist with mechanics if you choose.

But the **research, judgement, sourcing, examples and editorial accountability** should belong to Trading Guide.

