# My current release verdict

I would classify this version as:

> **Production Release Candidate — not Production Green yet.**

The code architecture is strong enough that I **would not recommend another major refactor**.

Your next work should be predominantly:

**verification → content quality → compliance → responsive/accessibility QA → production infrastructure → live SEO validation.**

The highest-value product strategy is also becoming clear:

> **Trading Guide should win through Australian trading education + transparent calculators + source-linked research, with comparisons as supporting functionality rather than the entire product.**

That is much more defensible than trying to outrank established comparison businesses by publishing another collection of “best broker” pages.

And because your site discusses financial products, I'd make the final compliance review a real launch requirement rather than relying on Terms/footer disclaimers: ASIC says the **overall impression and presentation** of the content matters when distinguishing factual information from financial-product advice. ([ASIC][7])

I have **not changed any source code in this audit**. The logical next implementation milestone is **Production Green Phase 1**, where we tackle the actual release gates one by one rather than adding new features.

